<title>USA: Va. Power nuke returns to 100 pct after test.</title>
<headline>Va. Power nuke returns to 100 pct after test.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Virginia Power Co's 781 megwawatt (MW) Surry 2 nuclear power plant in Gravel Neck, Va., has returned to full power Wednesday after being reduced to 45 percent on Tuesday, the company said.</p>
<p>&quot;It was a quarterly scheduled test of a turbine valve. We have returned to 100 percent power,&quot; said company spokesman Jim Norvelle, noting production at the unit was reduced for only a few hours.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit, with an identical generating capacity, is operating at full power.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
</text>
